 to test this old behavior. We don't test it anymore. Does it mean that we don't actually care what URL is displayed during pending time?"],["0b0c377f_de50d394",19,-1,1,"url1?"],["3b93d66f_b19f9671",19,-1,1,"I think this can be fixed? Not sure what is the issue here"],["8524c620_510b2877",19,-1,0,"should we unpause on tear down?"],["a248c26d_971090eb",19,-1,1,"Do you still need this one?"],["b49b4400_f0120e01",19,-1,1,"remove?"],["e97151db_3a03d9ea",19,-1,1,"url2?"]],0,1612],[7242605,20431,12,0.481,0.278,[[56,4]],[["1088155d_2ce2e0c3",20,0,1,"nit \\`CleanUpTitleForMatching()\\`"],["a222afa1_6ef44f96",20,0,1,"nit \\`kCleanedUpTitleMaxLength\\`"]],0,1613],[7241753,20432,1,0.142,0.092,[[4,85]],[],0,1614],[7254560,20437,8,0.037,0.015,[[17,79]],[],0,1615],[7260580,20437,2,0.088,0.061,[[9,88]],[],0,1615],[7255800,20438,50,1.21,0.931,[[65,0.596,3,32],[5,0.246,65,11],[3,0.105,742,5],[66,0.053,0,2]],[["38cecd88_05c66423",2,-1,1,"should we just leave this old weird key in place for now to minimize the changes in this CL?"],["509dc706_5efec437",21,-1,0,"instead of adding this helper, could we just convert callers to use failedNavigationURL and create the nsurl version instead when necessary?"],["5ca60a67_5ac82e01",2,-1,0,"missing the string version here? The dict used to have both"],["6b53f407_d0f3d8b1",22,-1,0,"The caller doesn't always need a mutable dictionary, so it seems a bit odd to require one. Consider just returning a dict directly. If the caller already has a mutable dict, it can add the returned…"],["7058110f_aae40ff4",22,-1,0,"If we wanted to get fancy, you could overload this function with a variant that takes a GURL and bake the conversion into the overload implementation."],["80dbba18_1fc169f4",23,-1,1,"using the other helper here would be more consistent with existing code. Even though it makes more sense to use the one which returns a URL instead of converting here, using the string key first…"],["82d56daa_d2fae70d",2,-1,1,"this is the wrong helper, it is making sure a string exists. However, this whole block from 684-701 is ALSO a workaround which may not be necessary anymore since your change on 722 to use…"],["8b5b63f0_c6441e68",22,-1,1,"I'm not sure this comment will make sense to folks in the future. Maybe add a note with a reference to the bug that some keys were missing and this was added as a workaround either here and/or in the…"],["9ecd2002_43c477f4",24,-1,1,"shouldn't this helper do this first, and then do the above conversion only if the NSURL key is missing?"],["a120e419_6d982e04",24,-1,0,"only default to other key if feature flag is set? (if Rohit still wants a flag)"],["a134f5c8_df459318",24,-1,1,"nit: can we add a TODO to remove this flag when we don't need it anymore?"],["c95de38b_73aaf839",2,-1,0,"This block will never get called anymore with this condition. I would leave the condition as it was before to be safest."],["ce2c6091_c2268631",24,-1,0,"This is changing behavior even if the flag is disabled. Overall, we should be more explicit about the code being the same as-is if the flag is disabled, even if that means a bit more…"],["f940c026_8f572071",25,-1,1,"Isn't there a GURL-to-NSURL conversion function?"],["140ea408_1992e919",2,0,0,"Same argument applies here too, right? We want to find the cases where the old key is missing and add it back."],["2f9c18a1_09899034",23,0,0,"Amazing."],["36a7757f_9a17ba7b",2,0,0,"This should be ok to update, no need to revert this part of the change."]],0,1616],[7265873,20440,168,3.848,3.085,[[65,0.41,4,73],[5,0.393,66,67],[3,0.12,743,18],[67,0.027,2,3],[36,0.027,4,4],[66,0.022,1,3]],[["3547aea6_377e1ee9",26,0,1,"nit: Moving user into to an intermediate variable may help readability here."],["94bfa7c0_cf407820",2,0,0,"```suggestion NSURL* URL = net::NSURLWithGURL(navigationContext->GetUrl()); ```"],["c3cd1703_9d247a19",2,0,0,"Should the comment be updated? Actually, is this whole block necessary?"]],0,1617]]}